# kurrent-firmware 0010: TLS 1.3 pre-shared-key client (firmware segment)
#
# Copyright (C) 2026 LECREATE <lecreate@foxmail.com>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# Adds a TLS 1.3 (RFC 8446) pre-shared-key client to the iPXE stack, so
# that the firmware boot segment can encrypt its own NVMe/TCP connection.
#
# src/net/tls.c and src/include/ipxe/tls.h supply the client-side
# handshake primitives: the RFC 8446 section 7.1 key schedule (labelled
# HKDF expansion, Derive-Secret, the Early / Handshake / Master secrets,
# traffic keys, the PSK binder and Finished), the ClientHello constructor
# (psk_dhe_ke, a single cipher suite and an X25519 key share), ServerHello
# parsing, the X25519 ephemeral key exchange, the handshake transcript
# context, and the RFC 8446 section 5.3 record protection (AEAD nonce,
# seal and open).  src/tests/tls13_test.c exercises all of this against
# the RFC 8448 test vectors.
#
# src/net/tls13.c and src/include/ipxe/tls13.h add the client connection
# itself: a filter interface inserted between a byte-stream consumer and
# the underlying socket, which drives the handshake and protects every
# subsequent record.  src/net/tcp/nvmetcp.c routes a session through it
# when nvmetcp_use_tls() holds, i.e. when the boot URI carries a tls_psk=
# parameter and the connection port equals tls_trsvcid (the handoff
# parameter is delivered on every TLS-capable boot, so the port, rather
# than the parameter's presence, decides whether the firmware connection
# itself is encrypted), deriving the "NVMe0R01 <hostnqn> <subsysnqn>" PSK
# identity.
#
# src/tests/tls13_conn_test.c exercises the connection layer in-process,
# with a mock socket and a mock consumer and with the test itself playing
# the server side of the handshake, so that the state machine, the record
# layer and the flow-control contract are covered without a network
# stack.  tls13_psk_open_socket() is the injection point for the mock
# socket; production code never reassigns it.
#
# All modified files carry FILE_LICENCE ( GPL2_OR_LATER_OR_UBDL ); the new
# self-tests (src/tests/tls13_test.c, src/tests/tls13_conn_test.c) follow
# the upstream self-test licensing.
#
# See blueprint/nvme-tcp-tls-in-firmware.md.

